    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0344" n="232" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/321</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-07T13:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 7, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Am informed by one of the spokesmen for movement referred to in my telegram of
                    January 25, 9 a.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d228-f1"/> that it will begin early
                    next week, that Turrichester [Turrialba] will be headquarters, that they possess
                    few resources but are going to make the attempt. Please see also my telegram of
                    December 31, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d228-f2"/> Am skeptical of success.
                    Reign of terror for Costa Ricans expected. Arrests continuing. Consul has
                    received two letters warning that he will be assassinated in order to bring
                    about intervention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
